<title>DENMARK: Danish shipping companies' earnings up in 1995.</title>
<headline>Danish shipping companies' earnings up in 1995.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish shipping companies' combined earnings rose to 5.7 billion crowns in 1995, a 21 percent rise from 1994's 4.7 billion, Denmarks National Statistics Office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Freight tonnage carried rose to 9.4 million tonnes gross from 8.2 million the year before but cargo earnings fell by three percent over the same period due to the weak dollar relative to the Danish crown, it said.</p>
<p>But dollar weakness helped reduce 1995 operating costs, by 1.3 billion crowns, due partly to lower chartering expenses. --Ole Mikkelsen, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33 969650</p>
